#!/bin/bash
# Fresh-state check, step 2 (plan phase 4): records whether the Cáptalo
# defaults domain exists; if it does, exports it to .local/shell/, flushes
# and verifies the copy by re-reading it, and only then deletes the domain.
# Touches only com.thecreativetoken.captalo. Quit Cáptalo first.
set -eu
. "$(dirname "$0")/defaults-common.sh"
STAMP=$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)
mkdir -p "$DIR"
require_quit
# One check at a time: a newer backup would hide the original values.
LAST=$(ls -t "$DIR"/defaults-*.state 2>/dev/null | head -1)
if [ -n "$LAST" ] && [ ! -e "${LAST%.state}.restored" ]; then
  echo "defaults-backup: $LAST is not restored yet; run make defaults-restore first" >&2
  exit 1
fi
if is_empty; then
  echo "absent" > "$DIR/defaults-$STAMP.state"
  echo "defaults-backup: domain absent; recorded $DIR/defaults-$STAMP.state"
  exit 0
fi
BACKUP="$DIR/defaults-$STAMP.plist"
defaults export "$DOMAIN" "$BACKUP"
sync
plutil -lint "$BACKUP" >/dev/null
if ! domain_matches "$BACKUP"; then
  echo "defaults-backup: verification failed; domain kept" >&2
  exit 1
fi
echo "present" > "$DIR/defaults-$STAMP.state"
defaults delete "$DOMAIN"
echo "defaults-backup: exported to $BACKUP and deleted the domain"
